Goal:
The password is base64 encoded and stored in a file in the home directory.

Approach:
My personal approach was to check the man page for base64 and see if there were any options that 
were there for decoding.

Command:
base64 -d data.txt

Breakdown:
base64 is a pre installed utility so the command is pretty straightforward.
We use base64 in the decode mode using the -d option and as the argument we specify the file we
want to decode.

Result:
" The password is pYfOY6HwUsDj5rL9U " it is not the complete password XD.

Key Takeaway:
base64 encoding and decoding was an interesting topic to study upon because of this room/level.

